## Structural Map

Key files Claude reads first:
- `CMakeLists.txt` — targets, flags, dependencies
- `src/main.cc` — entry point and wiring
- `src/` — modules, one header and source per unit
- `include/` — public headers
- `tests/` — GoogleTest / Catch2

Layers and their purpose:
- `src/api/` → Request parsing and validation, call into services
- `src/services/` → Business logic
- `src/storage/` → Database access through prepared statements
- `tests/` → Real-persistence-path tests for P1/P2 (see `cpp-patterns.md`)

