## Run / Test / Build

```bash
# Configure + build
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug && cmake --build build

# Test
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

# Sanitizers
cmake -S . -B build-asan -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="-fsanitize=address,undefined" && cmake --build build-asan && ctest --test-dir build-asan
```

## Known Gotchas

[Service-specific quirks. Examples:]
- **Raw buffers**: `strcpy`/`sprintf` on input are memory-safety bugs; use bounded APIs. See `cpp-patterns.md §Memory and Resource Safety`.
- **Size overflow**: check before multiplying lengths read from input.
- **Data races**: run ThreadSanitizer on concurrent code.
